Done. `parseFlags` now accepts `--DRY_RUN` (bare or with a value) alongside the existing flags, and `main` strips it before config validation. When present, it prints exactly one `dry-run port=... level=... capacity=...` line, returns `{ exitCode: 0, config }`, and never calls `createQueue`; invalid configs still emit the existing configuration error and return exit code 2. Added valid (bare and valued) plus invalid dry-run tests — `node --test` passes 31/31, and only `src/app.js` and `test/app.test.js` changed.
